package resource

import (
	_ "embed"
	"slices"
	"strings"
	"sync"
)

// reservedNamesRaw is a newline-separated, lowercased, byte-sorted list of
// notable public GitHub accounts (users + orgs) that must not be impersonable
// as Entire-native project names. Each entry is pruned to the canonical
// project-name shape — 3-32 chars, [a-z0-9-], no leading/trailing '-' — so it
// is a name a human could otherwise actually mint. This only gates
// human-created projects: system mirror projects skip CreateProject entirely
// and their "gh:mirrors:" names contain ':', which no entry here does.
//
// Regenerate with `mise run reserved-names`. The sort order is load-bearing —
// slices.BinarySearch relies on it, and reserved_names_test.go fails if the
// asset is ever out of order or carries an entry that isn't a valid project
// name.
//
// For where this list comes from — the source rankings and the curation logic
// behind it — see ephemera/tasks/20260616-cool-names.
//
//go:embed reserved_names.txt
var reservedNamesRaw string

// reservedNames is the sorted slice isReservedProjectName binary-searches. Built
// once, lazily, on first project create. strings.Split returns substrings that
// share reservedNamesRaw's backing array — no per-entry copy — so the whole set
// costs ~the asset size plus one slice header per line (~2.3MB for ~88k names).
var reservedNames = sync.OnceValue(func() []string {
	return strings.Split(strings.TrimSpace(reservedNamesRaw), "\n")
})

// isReservedProjectName reports whether name collides with a notable public
// account and must be refused. name must already be the canonical project-name
// shape — normalizeProjectName has shape-checked it (lowercase ASCII, [a-z0-9-],
// uppercase rejected outright), so it's in the same form as the asset entries

